DEFINITIONS USED
- M1/M2 slot value: plain mean over that slot's exam episodes of the family set (24 visible, 12 held-out);
  equal to the mean of family means because families have equal counts. Run value = mean of slots A and B.
- When the two final harnesses are identical the log carries the same report for both slots; both rows are used as logged.
- twin-stack-collective-r2: exam taken from exam_resit.jsonl, not log.jsonl.
- Seed level: mean of the 12 values in seed_exam.json 'visible' (for M1) and 'heldout' (for M2).
- 'within 0.10': absolute difference of arm means <= 0.10 (boundary counts as within).
- 'edit': the log's `edited` flag (candidate tree hash != the hash the candidate started from).
- P7 denominator: every turn whose outcome is not noop (invalid, boot_fail, regress, commit);
  discarded = invalid + boot_fail + regress. Two variants printed.
- P8: (mean M2 over 15 runs - seed held-out) >= 0.5 * (mean M1 over 15 runs - seed visible).
- Permutation p: all C(6,3)=20 relabellings, share with |diff| >= |observed|, ties included.
- Totals: end-row calls, usd, model_errors as logged; the resit's cost is shown apart.
